                <pb facs="0730" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.93/390: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi> (U. S. S. “<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Luzon</hi>”)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-27T13:00:00+08:00">November 27, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 27—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. My 1, November 22, 4 p.m. I arrived Hankow this morning. My colleagues have
                    also arrived. Minister for Foreign Affairs is expected here tomorrow. Two Vice
                    Ministers are already in Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
